The stereo layer is active only once the compositor took its declaration, and a failed declaration is said (ORDER 448). The layer attached and committed the two views of a 3D video even when the declaration of its surface as stereo content failed (a warning in the log only), and stereoLayerActive never looked at the declaration: the person saw the packed frame, both views side by side in each eye, while the player said 3D. The surface is now declared when the layer is made, before any buffer is attached to it, and a refusal is kept for the layer's life: a layer whose declaration failed attaches and commits nothing on any of its three routes (window surface, own DMA-BUF buffers, wl_shm), its presenter is not valid and says why, and VideoOutput does not use it. stereoLayerActive is then false, the item draws the video through the scene graph (one view, by stereoView), and the new read-only VideoOutput and Video property stereoLayerFailure holds the reason, with its change signal; the reason is also logged once (category qt.multimedia.video.stereolayer). It stays while the same 3D video plays, so the declaration is not asked for again at every frame, and clears when the 3D video ends or the item changes window: the next 3D video declares again.
